  <!-- Hero text under the page title -->
  <Fragment slot="lede">Natural hazards are becoming more frequent and severe in Seychelles as climate change progresses.</Fragment>

  <!-- Country context: shown in full -->
  <Fragment slot="context">
    <p>Natural hazards are becoming more frequent and severe in Seychelles as climate change progresses. Coastal degradation, limited water resources and biodiversity loss increase vulnerability, with climate-sensitive economic sectors, food security and health especially affected.</p>
    <p>RE2CLID works with national authorities and the Indian Ocean Commission on displacement-sensitive disaster risk management. A Technical Implementation Package for Seychelles was not included in the source pack, so this summary uses the cluster Description of the Action.</p>
  </Fragment>

